.nf
YASMV manual                                                 check

SYNOPSIS
  check init [options]
  check trans [-depth N] [options]
  check reachable EXPR [options]
  check invariant EXPR [options]
  check progress EXPR [options]

DESCRIPTION
.fi
Checks model consistency, reachability, safety, or universal eventual progress.
A validated model is required. init checks INIT and INVAR for satisfiability.
trans checks for a path of N transitions without INIT (default N=1); it does
not establish freedom from deadlocks. reachable asks whether some initialized
execution reaches EXPR. invariant checks EXPR in every reachable state.
progress requires every maximal execution to visit EXPR at least once:
non-goal dead ends and cycles violate it, and no fairness is assumed.

Operands are model expressions. Instead, use -name NAME to select a saved
property for invariant, or a saved goal for reachable/progress. Names never
implicitly shadow model symbols.

-method bmc|induction|interpolation applies to reachable and invariant.
Interpolation is the default and has no depth cap. BMC requires -depth N
(N=0..10000); induction requires -depth N (N=1..10000) for its base checks
and induction length. Interpolation rejects -depth. -shortest requires BMC.
A failed induction step can start in unreachable states and is not a concrete
counterexample. Bounded negative results never establish an unbounded proof.

-c EXPR adds an assumption (repeatable). BMC reachability also supports timed
path constraints @N{EXPR} and $N{EXPR}; all conclusions retain the constraints.
-wall-ms N (or unlimited), -conflicts N, and -propagations N bound work.
-states N applies only to progress. -sync and -async override execution mode.
Unsupported options and methods fail explicitly. Options use one dash; --
starts an SMV comment.

Default timeout, execution mode, and progress state limit come from settings.
Built-ins are 30s, sync, and 10000. Resource exhaustion is UNKNOWN, not a proof.
Use job wait to retrieve background results and select their validated traces;
job show -full displays the resolved request and complete evidence. dump-trace
inspects a selected witness. Failed checks preserve the current trace unless
they supply a replay-validated counterexample.

SEE ALSO
  help settings, help job, help property, help goal, help validate-progress.
